  "help_title": "TTTR Image Browser Help",
  "help_text": "TTTR Image Browser\n\nBrowse TTTR files in a folder and preview intensity images for all DetectorWizard-defined detector windows. The toolbar replaces the old inline buttons:\n\n\u2022 \ud83d\udcc2 Open: choose a folder containing TTTR images\n\u2022 \ud83e\uddf9 Clear: clear the current file list\n\u2022 \u267b\ufe0f Caches: clear in-memory and on-disk image caches\n\u2022 \ud83d\udce4 Export: copy selected raw image files\n\u2022 TIFF: export intensity images as TIFF stacks\n\u2022 DOCX: export selected images and annotations as a DOCX report\n\nThe GUI talks to the TTTR Image Browser backend through RPC for file listing, metadata, and image loading. The command line interface uses Click:\n\n  tttr-image-browser list FOLDER [--recursive]\n  tttr-image-browser load FILE [--max-side 512]\n  tttr-image-browser export-tiff FILE [FILE ...] --output-dir DIR\n  tttr-image-browser contract\n",
